{
  "date": "2026-09-22T07:37:40.648934+00:00",
  "issue": "Shared generic constructor seals a concrete field whose unbox still assumes unique ownership",
  "status": "Isolated candidate; not installed",
  "patch": "patches/bend-hot-constructor-fields.patch",
  "root_cause": "Global sharing makes Some hot. Constructing Some<Wide> seals Wide with an RFC wrapper, but the concrete Wide type was not marked hot if the value was immediately boxed without a typed binding. The cold Wide unbox then reads the RFC wrapper with term_loc and frees it in the Wide allocation class. This corrupts both values and allocator state.",
  "fix": "In emit_ctr, propagate an already-hot constructor through its concrete ADT with existing facts_hot. Analysis only grows hot facts and discards generated output until the fixed point, so earlier emitted cold unboxes are regenerated.",
  "scope": "One executable compiler line plus explanatory comment; no runtime change, generated-C workaround, or compiler installation.",
